<title>AUSTRALIA: Coles prefs convert to 57.27 mln shares.</title>
<headline>Coles prefs convert to 57.27 mln shares.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rretailer Coles Myer Ltd said on Friday that its converting preference shares had converted into 57.27 million ordinary shares effective June 5.</p>
<p>The company said trading in the new shares would commence on the ASX on a deferred settlement basis on June 10.</p>
<p>Coles shares had run up from a low on May 29 of A$5.96 to Thursday's high of A$6.40 prior to the conversion.</p>
<p>By 12.30 p.m. (0230 GMT), Coles Myer shares were two cents lower at A$6.29 on turnover of 3.45 million shares.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373 1800</p>
